Date: 2026-08-10

Mode: metric-led source/type classification; exact CPU/table algebra

## 1. Result first

The pinned complete-branch corpus already contains a nontrivial pattern, but it is a pattern of
**mathematical apparatus**, not a derived map of physical regimes.

Across all 24 stable branch identities and all six G54 measurement families, the 144-cell atlas
separates into 11 evidence-defined pattern families. Five branch/global-completion entries own a
restricted geometric relation type:

```text
R04  aggregate member-dependent relation type;
R17  path/holonomy relation type with conditional reciprocal assembly;
R18  clock-only endpoint relation type;
R23  complete-screen path/holonomy type without owned non-isometric scale;
R24  stratified set-valued projector type.
```

None owns the complete physical calibrated observer-pair relation. None selects optional
measurement coefficients or a physical regime label.

The strongest conditionally assembled panel remains R17. Once its complete calibrated pair
relation and path-carried state are supplied, `kappa`, `phi`, `beta`, and `U_gamma` are all
mathematically available and the founded reciprocal scalar is `Delta_phi`. The branch owns the
ingredients but not the chosen semidirect comparison law, physical path, carried-to-intrinsic
reset, or pair surface.

